<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hechingen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hechingen is a town in the Zollernalb district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, at the foot of the hill crowned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenzollern-castle">Hohenzollern Castle</a>. It was the seat of the Swabian counts of Zollern and, from 1576, of the Hohenzollern-Hechingen line, raised to princely rank in 1623, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> court was known for its music. The town passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> in 1850.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hechingen.jpg" alt="Hechingen" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muesse · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klosterkirche_St.Luzen_(Hechingen)_D%C3%A4cher.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
